-- EXPECT-LINES: 23 27
-- EXPECT-SOUND: 3
-- A block item at a column matching no open level, and a fault after it.
--
-- The layout filter, not the parser, catches this: an item line that is
-- neither deeper than the current level nor equal to any open one is L6, and
-- it is repaired by adopting the column so the block skeleton survives.
--
-- The first line NUMBER here is deliberate and worth reading twice: the fault
-- is blamed on line 15, the line being CONTINUED, not line 16, the one that is
-- over-indented. A layout token has length zero, so wok_parse.c's `blame`
-- charges it to the end of the last thing the author actually wrote -- which is
-- where a missing `=` or `->` belongs. Do not "fix" this to point at line 16
-- without reading that rule; E1 chose it on purpose.
--
-- What this pins: the repair is LOCAL, and exactly local. The case comes back
-- with all THREE alternatives -- H_Alt, E_Error, H_Alt -- so the damaged one
-- became an error node IN PLACE and both neighbours survived. The enclosing
-- equation still parses, and the independent fault later is still reported.
module M

pick cmd = case cmd of
  0 -> 1
   1 -> 2
  2 -> 3

after y := 9

last = 10
